{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1084494-double-double-toil-and-trouble-alchemical-witchcraft","id":1084494,"title":"Double, Double, Toil, and Trouble: Alchemical Witchcraft","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-27T08:24:27-07:00","id":1084494,"title":"Double, Double, Toil, and Trouble: Alchemical Witchcraft","content":"So I've a friend, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, who's got a cool concept in mind: basically your mythological hag witch. The kind that eat children and brew potions. Sadly, there aren't really rules for brewing potions of any strength. I've looked through the books, and I think the pieces are all there: mortal sorcery from The Fall of Isireion, Alchemists from Promethean, and Esoteric Armory. Ideally this would be a way to create small-scale potions: nothing big enough to count as a Supernatural Merit (so the splats could enjoy some toil and trouble too).<br /> <br /> How would y'all craft rules for such a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:22:09-07:00","id":1084543,"title":"","content":"You might look at the Ascending Ones, too. They are a primarily alchemy-oriented Hunter conspiracy. The Experience cost for things was too high but it's something that could be edited away easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:28:48-07:00","id":1084547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1084494-double-double-toil-and-trouble-alchemical-witchcraft?p=1084543#post1084543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might look at the Ascending Ones, too. They are a primarily alchemy-oriented Hunter conspiracy. The Experience cost for things was too high but it's something that could be edited away easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew my lack of Hunter knowledge would get in my way someday. Are they in the core book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:32:26-07:00","id":1084553,"title":"","content":"They are, they're one of the core conspiracies, and there's more info and elixirs in every other Hunter book too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:47:30-07:00","id":1084569,"title":"","content":"Also, doesn't Chronicles of Darkness Core have options for simple magic charms and such through the Occult skill and Equipment rules? You could look into expanding those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:10:57-07:00","id":1084621,"title":"","content":"I always associate that kind of magic with Hedgespinning from CtL: collecting ingredients, physical and abstract, in order to weave their stories into a spell.<br /> <br /> In CtL it makes hedgespun items, and requires an object pulled put of a dream as a core, so it would need some tweaking, but it has the right feel / style for magic from myths and stories, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:42:14-07:00","id":1084639,"title":"","content":"You could check out a combination of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\">Hedge Sorcerers</a> (to get the Contracts) and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits#post841832\">Witch's Brew</a> merit (for making them into a potion). <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/864954-primordial-sorcery-homebrew\">Primordial Sorcery</a> (specifically, the Enchanting school) is also worth a look.<br /> <br /> And take a look at the new Alpha doc for Endowments in the Hunter sub-forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:49:37-07:00","id":1085454,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to do it would just be using the structure Rites from Fall of Iseiron, with the effect always being a physical object with the desired property, and instead of a point of Pillar, use a point of Pyros to skip a step.<br /> <br /> For example, you could have an Alchemical &quot;Rite&quot; that produces a youth serum, and requires multiple alchemical reagents and the blood of a child, but Pyros can skip the blood requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T15:05:44-07:00","id":1085603,"title":"","content":"I've always been a fan of Alchemy. Generally, Promethean has a few interesting things you might want to take a look at regarding concepts etc.<br /> What type of Alchemy are you thinking, though?<br /> For there a worlds of difference between e.g. the system you see in Skyrim, where certain ingredients have certain properties and you can just mess around trying to figure out something good, and the Witcher system, with potions being generally toxic and you need to be trained on how to make use of them (the Ascending One's had this going for them a lot), but limited to some fixed recipes, and all other attempts at potions are simply bad.<br /> <br /> What do you want these potions to be able to achieve? Far-Sight? Strength/Speed-Buff? Polymorph-Juice? Luck-Potion? Skinabsorbend poison? Mind-Control agents spread via ChemTrails?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the set system a la Ascending Ones is easier to use, but keeping it completely freestyle/fluff might be more fun AND would be more an activity similar to hacking a computer or running away (Occult+Int, maybe?), which would be more in tune with the 'not a supernatural merit' idea.<br /> You could go for a point-based system for simple stuff like enhancers - every bonus point it nets is a success you need to get within the time you prepare the mixture. Assume standard values whenever everything else would be too complicated.<br /> A basic potion would have something like doubling your speed for 10 turns, needing 19 successes (standard speed is 9 iirc). The resultant score would be how many successes have to be rolled to brew the mixture. Shortening/lenghtening the timespan and/or increasing/decreasing the effect would accordingly change the neccessary amount of successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> What might be more fun would be a largely symbolic-based system: As ST, you'd have a few possible recipies with what can be achieved prepared in advance and marked with points for how difficult they are/ how long they work etc. what type of ingredients are needed, and which kind of ingredients are absolutely necessary. Some ingredients would bring a beneficial, others a harmful side effect. Typical factors would be container used, style of preperation, choice and number of ingredients and circumstances (daytime/nightime etc.).<br /> What makes this fun imo is seeing what the players choose to use, and how they justify it.<br /> <br /> Example 1: I want to make a simple strength enhancing spell giving me the strength of 10 men (maybe I wanna open a certain heavy gate to prove myself worthy or somesuch). As this would add at least 20 Strength (let's be literal here for a moment), this would be very powerful, so I'd have to search for accordingly rare/powerful ingredients. Iron is strong, so I might pick a iron bowl as the container of where to mix that stuff, but since its not rare or anything, it wouldn't do much. A warrior's helmet, on the other hand... An accomplished historical fighter's helmet (succesful famous viking, long-time winner of gladiator fights etc.)? Even better. Hair of a bear or boar collected from a live specimen up close (read active, wild and strong, not sedated/tame) or maybe feathers of an eagle, gunpowder (explosive strength), an oaken (strong wood) spoon and stamped during the night under the full moon (requires more physical work than cooking) and voila, done is the shortlived superstrength-granting balm.<br /> However, werewolf saliva (gathered from a Gauru) might be an even more potent than animal hair and increase duration/strength or add something like total restoration from Bashing/Lethal. Using Eagle's feathers rather than the other things might induce increased speed rather than strength. Using Lion's hair could cause induce a bout of extreme pride and thus inflict the overconfident condition. Cooking up the whole thing under the waning moon would <b>sap </b>strength, as would using a tamed/sedated animal, the waxing moon would instead delay the onset of the potion and turn it into a growing and then ebbing effect rather than an immediate power-up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Example 2: For the aforementioned Youth Serum, lets make it a thing that gives you back years of your life (not necessarily extending your life span, just whipping your body back to shape). You would need a iron or lead couldron (base) for the cooking, but a gold cup (everlasting/noble) to drink from to symbolize the perfection attempted, and a wooden spoon (formerly living material) to stir, water (source of life), fire (heat=&gt; source of life), and cooked during full daylight (the ingredients of life), and then something like organs like hearts, brains and liver, blood etc. (symbolic value stressed). The blood of a child would take off decades, runes spelling 'Life everlasting' or somesuch on the couldron/cup could add a bonus to the duration. Using something like an old hen's blood would instead add a frailty of old age via a condition, using mercury (often considered a neccessary ingredient in eternal-life-potions historically speaking) could introduce a side effect (possibly benefitial, possibly harmful, always unexpected).<br /> <br /> This of course could change the whole Alchemy thing into a side-quest or even storyline in and of itself, so I don't know if this is what you're looking for. These are fun, but then, maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> I guess this isn't very helpful in regards to preexisting systems, though. Sorry I got sidetracked. Hope I still was able to add something to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}